      "author": "@RuthShelton-ou4id",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/Mx35rszCkRPJ_Vbv1UP3pR3TkfKcVTR356d48jOJdEVbFKWT7YCqwHJHHbvOM6QXSYmd7bg9uw=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "Hello from the 1700 historic town of Maryland.👋😎\n   🛥️ Chesapeake 🛥️\n  I don't believe that 'death' of our bodies means a total ending-- What truly runs our bodies - our sprite- just moves on. \n  Whatever happens at 'death' each of us will find out all in our time. \n  We would visit & sing for folks in a nursing home & a picture was taken showing a black cat on the lap of a lady there -- except when the picture was taken the cat wasn't seen-- \nThe lady once had a black cat that she truly loved -- & latter that day we found out that nice lady had passed away. I think the cat helped her pass over--?\n   The coffins being found having moved around -- bazaar!!\n   Why weren't the parents buried next to the child afraid of lightning? Maybe they moved out of town-- who knows",
      "likeCount": 2,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-03T17:35:27Z",
      "replyCount": 0,
      "replies": []
    },
